//     18    a practitioner, or a sourced technique, for lighting and exposing darker skin; written
//           only as far as Luckiesh's reflectance principle and DI0370's two meter readings
//     20    BAM's demonstration of matching a lamp in the shot by its box
//     22    a theater lighting designer or electrician
//     23    a television lighting director or studio engineer
//     24    a gaffer or set electrician; does not ship without one and stays a link lesson until then
//   Each P lesson is written only as far as the documents carry it and says, under "Where the
//   practitioner's part begins" or "Where BAM's demonstration begins", where that part takes over.
//   Unmarked: 1, 2, 4, 6, 11 (the practice drill), 12, 14, 19.
//
// RIGHTS (the source-hosting rule in CLAUDE.md, decided per source):
//  - Tier A, may be hosted on Cloudinary later: Fuchs 1929, Ridge 1928, Luckiesh 1916 and 1920 (both),
//    Selden and Sellman 1930 (the 1930 scan only, never the later printings), Powell 1923, Duchochois
