//    the U.S. Department of Labor, Employment and Training Administration).
//  - Tier B, link only, never rehost: the ETCP pages.
//  - Copyrighted standards: ESTA/ANSI E1 entertainment standards and NFPA 70 (the National Electrical
//    Code) are cited by name and linked to their listing pages only if a reviewer adds them, never
//    reproduced; none is quoted here. Tier C books (Brown, Cinematography; Tucker 2023; Brook 1968;
//    Bogart 2001) are not used.
//  - FIGURES: none embedded. TM 11-401-2 Fig. 9-9, Luckiesh 1916 Fig. 108 and Fuchs's p. 99 face
//    figure are described in words and cited by number and page (the Luckiesh and Fuchs images were
//    not viewed, so only their captions are used).
//
// FATALITY CASE: the only one in this course's dossier is CPSC's 1996 report of 30 fires and two
// deaths with tubular halogen torchiere lamps (lesson 25), a federal aggregate with no victim or
// incident named, so no news coverage was fetched. The stage-light-tower ballast death (Massachusetts
// FACE 19MA072) belongs to CREW-01 lesson 17 and is linked from lesson 22, not retold.
//
// STANDARDS: unmapped for now (BACKLOG entry in scripts/check-standards-coverage.ts). NGSS waves and
// light (PS4) or a CTE technical-theater standard are the candidates once a reviewer has read it.
//
// HEDGES WRITTEN INTO LESSONS (each needs a check in src/lib/research-checks.ts; the report that
// accompanies this draft quotes each sentence):
//  - L2: BLS figures read only through O*NET; why O*NET's "gaffer" search matches 27-4015.00; ETCP's
