//  - L10: no safe distance between a modern lamp and a card, sheet or cloth.
//  - L14: "golden hour", "magic hour" and "blue hour" have no definition in the dossier.
//  - L18: no source for lighting and exposing darker skin.
//  - L20: whether every household lamp is a "general service lamp"; DI0370's 3,200 K and 5,600 K.
//  - L21: how LED sources behave when dimmed.
//  - L22: how a lighting plot is drawn.
//  - L23: a current camera's contrast range.
//  - L24: crew titles, power distribution and current film-set practice.
//  - L25: LED fixture heat; DI0370's cooling time.
//  - L26: whether a show is a "similar purpose" under 1910.305(a)(2)(i); who counts as a qualified
//    person for set power; load arithmetic.
//
// House style, matching stage-and-broadcast-rigging-course.ts and sound-craft-course.ts: `section` on
// every lesson; flush-left single-line `:::reveal q ||| a`; recallContent from the second teaching
// lesson on, quizzing the teaching lesson before; an APA 7 `## Sources` block on every teaching lesson
// with a locator on every entry (CFR paragraph; printed page AND PDF page where they differ: Fuchs PDF
// = printed + 5 early in the book and + 4 in Appendix E, Luckiesh 1916 PDF = printed + 20, Luckiesh
// 1920b PDF = printed + 32 at pp. 225 to 227, TM 11-401-2 and DI0370 as given per page); a quiz per
// section pooled to round(words / 35), clamped 40 to 100, serving 5, passing 80, shuffled; a final
// pooling 40+ and serving 10, placed last. Option lengths are balanced within each question so the
// correct option is neither visibly the longest nor the shortest. American spelling in prose;
// quotations keep their own spelling. No em or en dashes anywhere: where a source prints a dash, the
// quotation is split at it. Every number is multiple choice; the one typed drill (lesson 11) asks
